Implement a dedicated rules-validation layer.

Example:

ClaimRuleEngine

Each check should produce a structured result rather than returning only True/False.

Example:

{
“rule”: “warranty_expiry”,
“passed”: true,
“severity”: “info”,
“message”: “Claim was submitted within the active warranty period.”,
“evidence”: {
“purchase_date”: “…”,
“claim_date”: “…”,
“warranty_expiry”: “…”
}
}

Implement at minimum the following checks.

1. Warranty Expiry

Validate:

claim_date <= warranty_expiry

Warranty expiry should derive from:

purchase date
+
applicable warranty duration

Handle malformed and missing dates safely.

