PHASE 18 — DUPLICATE DETECTION

Build two duplicate-detection mechanisms.

A. Document Duplicate Detection

For every uploaded document calculate:

SHA256(file_bytes)

Store hashes in the database.

Do not hash filenames or temporary paths.

Hash the actual file contents.

Use an indexed database column for document hashes where appropriate.

When a file is uploaded:

1. calculate SHA256
2. check whether the same hash already exists
3. identify associated claims
4. create a duplicate warning when relevant

Do not automatically reject a claim solely because a document hash exists elsewhere.

There may be legitimate reused documents.

Return enough information for reviewer investigation.

Never leak another claimant’s private data to an unauthorized customer.

Reviewer/admin visibility must respect RBAC.

